    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No furosemide-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement in visible L6 records.",
    "No direct oral versus intravenous absolute F measurement for furosemide or a close analog.",
    "No fed-state-specific furosemide absorption or bioavailability data.",
    "Azosemide and bumetanide records are analog, in vitro, or rat assays with low transferability to human oral F.",
    "No furosemide-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism measurement in visible records."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds hepatic clearance and metabolic stability records for other molecules, including azosemide rat microsomal intrinsic clearance and bumetanide low hepatic extraction, but no furosemide-specific result. These analog/in vitro records are low-transferability mechanistic context, not affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20%. Transferable high-F contexts, including fed-state safinamide F=95.3%, continue to support F >= 20%. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

